 # AIRK documentation
 
-**1.8.7:** CLI and Workbench reads use the MCP handlers and retain their full results, including configured `query_concurrency` in status/diagnostics. Cold status preserves explicit setup-timeout receipts across later polls. This release consolidates all unpublished 1.8.0-1.8.6 storage, startup, retrieval, concurrency and Workbench improvements. See the [consolidated release notes](releases/release-1.8.7.md) for current behavior and dated validation.
+**1.8.8 is an unpublished manual-test working build.** Accepted local P9–P12 work adds permanent exclusions, reviewed index splitting, per-file profile reporting, explicit Lean/Rich retained profiles and reviewed reference refresh with separate requery. P13 retains current ranking and diversity. P14 selected local qualification includes Windows native tests and documented editor coverage. Manual acceptance and release promotion remain separate. See the [working-build record](releases/release-1.8.8.md) and [implementation ledger](research/implementation-v190.md) for exact evidence, failures and platform limits.
 
-Unreleased developer workflow: [native build reuse and Darwin failure diagnostics](ci-and-builds.md#native-build-reuse-and-darwin-failure-diagnostics) describes the separate build/validation jobs, complete-attempt release rule, focused repetitions and remaining Intel failure. Product versions remain synchronized at 1.8.7.
+Opening a trusted folder does not register or index it. Use **Indexing > Index library** to review sources, storage and watching; create Project memberships and review an access grant, then explicitly **Use Grant for this window**. Evidence reads and source verification do not start indexing.
 
-Developer references: [MCP tools](mcp-developer-guide.md) covers all 28 public tools with inputs, examples, evidence limits and implementation/test links. [CLI commands](cli-developer-guide.md) covers each command, its purpose, native ownership and guarded workflows. Both explain why `airk tools list` has 18 native tools while unified MCP has 28, and map the remaining capabilities to separate terminal commands.
+**Setup and uninstall:** Successful setup or reconnection clears obsolete failure warnings. Current setup failures remain visible, and uninstall removes empty shell startup files that AIRK created. See [setup and uninstall guidance](vscode-extension.md).
+
+**Missing sources and storage:** the working source adds [reviewed index
+retirement and cleanup](service-project-retirement.md) for removed files or folders and separate
+[unavailable legacy-index upgrade recovery](service-installation.md#unavailable-legacy-index-during-upgrade). Healthy indexes keep
+their independent evidence; old grants are never silently narrowed. Post-P14
+recovery has selected Windows native/process and Mac portable validation. Full
+workspace and final installer qualification remain separate; see the working-build
+record for current results and earlier failures.
+
+| Current guide | Scope |
+| --- | --- |
+| [Source verification and explicit reference refresh](source-verification.md) | Dated read-only verification; separately reviewed P12 refresh/requery and its limits |
